 urnalists is open for its 2027 round. Fellows spend twelve months working 
 part-time and remotely with a personal mentor\, reporting and writing arti
 cles about the craft of science journalism that are published at The Open 
 Notebook\, one of the field's central craft resources. Eligibility: early-
 career science journalists with fewer than three years of regular professi
 onal science-writing experience\; applicants from anywhere in the world ar
 e welcome\, and application materials are in English. TO APPLY: submit the
  application form (linked from the program page) by 31 October 2026\, 11:5
 9 PM US Central time\; reference letters are due 7 November 2026. The fell
 owship year starts 9 February 2027.\n\nOrganisation: The Open Notebook\nLo
 cation: Remote\, worldwide. Application materials in English\; internation
 al applicants welcome.\nAward: USD 6\,600 stipend over the twelve-month pa
 rt-time fellowship\, plus one-on-one mentoring from an experienced science
  journalist and published clips at The Open Notebook. No application fee.\
